Switch: the deko3d NRO records Aurora's frames into deko3d (AURORA_GFX_DEKO3D)

docs/DEKO3D_MIGRATION_PLAN.md phase 3, on top of 0013. With AURORA_GFX_DEKO3D (the deko3d NRO) Aurora's
recorded frames go to switch/deko/aurora (dk_gfx.hpp) instead of Dawn's encoders; Dawn's Null device stays
the object model (its textures, views, samplers and bind groups get deko3d shadows through the linker's
--wrap, switch/deko/aurora/dk_objects.cpp):
- frame.cpp: the staging buffers are deko3d memory (dk::staging_create) that the FIFO thread writes and
  the GPU reads in place: one more than the frame slots, "mapped" once the GPU has finished their frame
  (dk::staging_ready); the shared WebGPU buffers shrink to 64 KiB (only the Null device's bind groups
  use them); the begin-frame item opens the deko3d frame (dk::frame_begin), the end-frame item notes the
  slot's frame after the present (dk::frame_presented); no draw census;
- encoding.cpp: encode_op hands each sealed op to dk::encode_op (no staging copies);
- recording.cpp: an upload larger than the frame's staging goes to deko3d memory of its own
  (dk::overflow_upload, TextureUpload::dkBlock/dkGpu), and detail::draw_kind tells the encoder a GX draw
  from a partial-clear draw;
- pipeline_cache: CompiledPipeline carries the deko3d pipelines (dkMain, dkPrepass), built on the compile
  thread by dk::build_gx_pipeline / dk::build_clear_pipeline (DKSH from the caches, or Tint + uam for a
  miss); gx::pipeline_state_desc gives the GX fixed state build_pipeline gives Dawn; dual-source blending
  only with COS_DK_DUAL_SOURCE=1 (dk::dual_source_blending), else the alpha prepass;
- resource_cache: find_bind_group_raw for the encoder (no reference counting per draw);
- aurora.cpp: end_frame presents through switch/deko only (the frame was recorded and submitted along
  the way).
Without AURORA_GFX_DEKO3D (the GL NRO, the Mac) nothing changes.

Switch only (switch/native/aurora/patches); not for upstream.

